{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788354838,"nonce":"L8nn0OgQiujnSnr+em7Se9ewkf4=","message":"**Implemented, worker, repair round 2026-09-02.** Branch\n`fix/a1644d6-enclosure`, commit `b5b8c5d` (it stands alone — the tree at that\ncommit builds without the `a1644d6` commit on top, checked). Source only, no\nassembly. Not run against a bench by me.\n\n\n**Item 1 — the rollup comes off the beds.** `room.Owners` is no longer called\nanywhere in `PlaceVerbs.cs`. `owners` / `owners_total` are built from\n`ContainedBeds` → `OwnersForReading`, the same route the `beds[]` block already\nused and got right, so the two cannot disagree: there is one route.\n`owners_total` is DISTINCT pawns, not bed-slots — a double bed lists the same\ntwo owners on both halves and this is a headcount.\n\n**Item 2 — and the disagreement is now structurally impossible rather than\nwarned about.** The comment's first branch, per the resolution above. The bare\ncatches are gone too, both of them: the rollup's catch emits a\n`Journal.EmitWarning` and publishes `owners_error` (presence is the signal, so\nits absence is the news), and the per-bed catch in `room`'s `beds[]` loop emits\none naming the bed. As the resolution says, that alone would have changed\nnothing — it is the latent hazard, not this bug.\n\n**Item 3 — a zero is now readable.** This was the real defect: `owners_total: 0`\nwas indistinguishable from an unclaimed barracks, and no key in the envelope\ncould tell them apart. Added: `beds_total` (uncapped), `beds_owned`,\n`owners_more`, and `owners_source: \"contained-beds\"` naming the route\nPawnSafe-style. So an empty room reads `0/0/0`, three unclaimed beds read\n`owners_total:0, beds_total:3, beds_owned:0`, and a barracks reads\n`owners_total:3, beds_owned:3`. Medical and prisoner beds were already flagged\nper-bed and stay so.\n\n**One thing I fixed that was not on the issue.** `room`'s `beds[]` list is