e from.\n- **Phase 9 (`--selftest`, offline, 11 checks, PASSES today)** runs over the\n  envelope THIS ISSUE banked, verbatim. Room 38 names three distinct owners\n  across three separately owned beds while publishing `owners_total: 0`; the\n  suite's own invariant FAILS on it and PASSES on the same envelope repaired,\n  which is the only honest way to show phase 1 checks anything. It also closes\n  the absent-vs-null trap: the banked envelope has no `owners_source` and no\n  `beds_total`, `eq(...,None)` passes on both, `shape()` does not.\n\nBench phases 0-3 were NOT run — no bench was launched.\n\n\nCommented on `664e9b9` separately.\n\n\nNo bed-ownership verb exists in the surface (`assign` is policies), which is\nwhy the acceptance stages ownership by letting colonists claim beds rather than\nissuing it. That is also how run `m1-20260901` got three owned beds without ever\nmaking an `assign` call — the vanilla auto-claim path — so the fixture is the\nreal one.","files":null}]}